      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's the concern. If we go the \"transparency\" route and explicitly call it out as a major limitation, I'm worried the reviewers will just use it as an excuse to reject the whole thing immediately. We really need this to get through the first round. \n\nIs there a way we can frame the methodology so it doesn't look like a weakness? Like, can we position the small N as a deliberate choice for depth or something, rather than just a limitation we're apologizing for?",
